WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.362
The second half covers the
changes that need the most care.

2
00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:08.068
Anything with a big blast radius, like
a tenant-wide role or a Conditional

3
00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:12.774
Access change, stays gated permanently,
however mature the program gets.

4
00:00:12.774 --> 00:00:17.262
Changes to the record itself are always
a human decision through review.

5
00:00:17.262 --> 00:00:19.746
Routine certificates run on protocol,

6
00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:22.850
and emergencies act first
and record afterward.

7
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.775
Two rules hold across all of it.

8
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:28.611
A machine never edits the
record to make drift disappear,

9
00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:31.713
and no gap quietly goes
to a person at a console.

10
00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:34.920
Now let's look at drift from
the other side, by class.
